      "content": "i hear what you're saying about \"no evidence,\" but that's kind of the point with covert monitoring, right? it's supposed to look natural. but if you actually look at the physics, those peace lilies have those broad, flat leaves that act like perfect parabolic reflectors if they're angled right. and the snake plants are tall and stiff, almost like acoustic baffles. \n\nif i wanted to set up a system like that without anyone knowing, what kind of specific geometric patterns or spacing would i need between the plants to maximize the collection of sound from the center of the room? like, is there a specific mathematical layout that would make that arrangement most effective at directing sound to a single point?",
